license: MIT

abstract: >
  An explainable and fair machine-learning framework for dynamic
  expected-loss optimization in credit risk. Built on the public Lending Club
  loan dataset, the project combines predictive modeling with
  interpretability and fairness analysis to support transparent, responsible
  credit decision-making. It extends the author's earlier comparative study of
  traditional and explainable AI approaches to credit risk modeling by adding
  dynamic expected-loss optimization and fairness evaluation. The project
  demonstrates end-to-end data science and financial engineering skills for
  educational and portfolio purposes.

keywords:
  - credit risk
  - expected loss
  - machine learning
  - explainable AI
  - XAI
  - fairness
  - financial engineering
  - Lending Club
  - data science
  - python

